The '''Nikto hideout''' was an encampment located on the [[desert]] world [[Arvala-7]] that was controlled by a [[Unidentified Nikto mercenary gang|gang]] of [[Nikto]] [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] in [[9 ABY]], guarding an [[Youngling|infant]] named [[Din Grogu|Grogu]]. At that [[time]], the [[bounty hunter]]s [[IG-11]] and [[Din Djarin]] raided the encampment during their [[Mission to Arvala-7|search]] for Grogu. After the two [[Hunting|hunters]] eliminated the mercenaries, IG-11 attempted to [[Death|terminate]] Grogu, but he was destroyed by Djarin, who took the infant into his custody. Sometime afterward, [[Kuiil]], a [[Moisture farmer|vapor farmer]], took IG-11's body from within the encampment and traveled back to his [[Kuiil's moisture farm|farm]] to repair the [[IG-series|droid]].

==Description==
[[File:Arvala-7.png|thumb|right|250px|The encampment was located on Arvala-7.]]
Located on the [[desert]] [[planet]] of [[Arvala-7]],<ref name="Handbook">''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian Handbook]]''</ref> the [[Nikto]] hideout<ref name="Audio Description Chapter 7">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 7: The Reckoning}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> was a small frontier [[City|town]]<ref name="Audio Description Chapter 1" /> surrounded by [[mountain]]s.<ref name="Chapter 1" /> The flat-roofed buildings making up the encampment were rectangular in arrangement and [[Color|brown]] in color. The area they enclosed was a dusty, open plaza<ref name="Junior Novel">[[The Mandalorian Junior Novel|''The Mandalorian'' Junior Novel]]</ref> that featured [[moisture vaporator]]s, a well, crates and barrels that were scattered about, and an abandoned [[speeder]].<ref name="Chapter 1" />

The encampment's innermost building had a brown<ref name="Chapter 1" /> security gate that was operated by an outdated security panel and an access pad,<ref name="Junior Novel" /> the wiring of which could be modified to allow entry into the building, though the gate itself could also be taken down by a<ref name="Chapter 1" /> heavy-[[artillery]] [[laser cannon]].<ref name="Junior Novel" /> The innermost building's interior included a large room with a clutter of objects,<ref name="Chapter 1" /> including storage crates and packaging that were strewn against the walls<ref name="Junior Novel" /> and across the floor.<ref name="Chapter 1" /> The [[Atmosphere|air]] within the building smelled old and stale.<ref name="Junior Novel" />

==History==
===The territory of mercenaries===
{{Quote|Since these ones arrived, this territory has been an endless stream of mercenaries seeking reward and bringing destruction.|Kuiil, to Djarin, pointing out the Niktos in the area|audio=KuiilMercs-TMS01CH01.flac|<ref name="Chapter 1" />}}
[[File:IG-11-Compound-DB.jpg|thumb|left|300px|IG-11 attacks the mercenaries in the encampment.]]
At some point, a [[Unidentified Nikto mercenary gang|gang]] of Nikto<ref name="Handbook" /> [[Mercenary|mercenaries]]<ref name="Chapter 1" /> gained control of the encampment,<ref name="Handbook" /> guarding within its innermost building an [[Youngling|infant]]<ref name="Chapter 1" /> known as [[Din Grogu|Grogu]],<ref name="Chapter 13">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 13: The Jedi}}</ref> who had a [[bounty]] placed on him. Many individuals, assisted by the [[Ugnaught]] [[Moisture farmer|vapor farmer]] [[Kuiil]], attempted to make their way to the area while seeking the infant, only to [[Death|die]] before they could claim the bounty.<ref name="Chapter 1" /> In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[The Mandalorian Season One|''The Mandalorian'' Season One]] to [[9 ABY]].</ref> during the [[New Republic Era]], the [[assassin droid]] [[bounty hunter]] [[IG-11]] entered the encampment and ordered the Nikto to obey the [[Bondsman Guild Protocol]], which dictated that the mercenaries were to produce the bounty for the [[IG-series|droid]]. When the mercenaries began attacking IG-11, the [[droid]] retaliated, forcing the mercenaries to temporarily retreat inside the buildings. Scouting the place with a [[scope]], the [[Mandalorian]] bounty [[Hunting|hunter]]<ref name="Chapter 1" /> [[Din Djarin]],<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref> who also wished to claim the bounty and was helped by Kuiil, [[Mission to Arvala-7|arrived]] at the scene and told IG-11 to stand down. Instead, the droid shot Djarin on sight, knocking the Mandalorian to the ground.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

After Djarin got up and convinced the droid to work with him in return for splitting the reward for the bounty, the mercenaries stormed out of the buildings and fired upon the duo. During the gunfight, Djarin and IG-11 took cover behind the abandoned speeder before hiding behind the pillars of the building where Grogu was kept. IG-11 covered Djarin as he attempted to bypass the building's security panel by accessing its wiring, but it was then destroyed by the Niktos' blaster fire, forcing the Mandalorian to take cover once again.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

===Bounty hunters triumphant===
{{Quote|We'll bring it in alive.''"<br />"''The commission was quite specific. The asset was to be terminated.|Djarin and IG-11 discuss how to handle Grogu after discovering him|audio=DjarinIG-11-Grogu-TMS1C1.flac|<ref name="Chapter 1" />}}
While the pair were pinned down, the mercenaries brought forth a [[Hoverturret|hovering]]<ref name="Chapter 1" /> heavy-artillery [[E-Web heavy repeating blaster cannon]]<ref name="PostGCW">{{EncyclopediaCite|Post-Galactic Civil War and the Mandalorian}}</ref> and fired upon the bounty hunters' position. However, the hunters were able to eliminate all of the mercenaries when IG-11 distracted the cannon's operator, allowing Djarin to hijack it and use the [[weapon]] against them. The pair subsequently entered the building where Grogu was located by using the cannon to destroy the structure's security gate.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

[[File:The_Mandalorian_and_the_Asset.png|thumb|right|300px|Djarin destroyed IG-11 and saved Grogu, taking the infant with him.]]
Upon entering the building, Djarin shot a Nikto who attempted to fire upon them. He then proceeded to open the [[Hover pram|hovering pram]] containing their target, and the pair discovered that it was in fact an infant. Adhering to the instructions he had been given, IG-11 attempted to terminate Grogu but was quickly shot in the head and destroyed by the Mandalorian, who took Grogu into his custody in order to return him to his [[The Client|client]].<ref name="Chapter 1" /> Sometime after the skirmish, Kuiil entered the encampment and retrieved IG-11's body from within, taking the droid's flotsam back to his [[Kuiil's moisture farm|farm]] to rebuild him.<ref name="Chapter 7">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 7: The Reckoning}}</ref> At some point after the [[Battle of Mos Espa]]<ref name="Secrets of the Bounty Hunters">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Bounty Hunters]]''</ref> that took place in the same [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="BoBF Date">{{BoBFDate}}</ref> the [[Weequay]] [[pirate]] [[Hondo Ohnaka]] wrote a [[book]] titled ''[[The Secrets of the Bounty Hunters]]''. It included an illustration of Djarin and IG-11's encounter with Grogu in the hideout that was featured in a section on IG-series droids.<ref name="Secrets of the Bounty Hunters" />

==Behind the scenes==
===Appearance and conception===
{{Quote|So, we came up with the idea that this was an old abandoned mining town nestled into these canyons. The bandits found it very convenient because, strategically, it was hidden and easier to defend.|Doug Chiang|<ref name="Art of Mandalorian S1">[[The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian (Season One)|''The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season One]]</ref>}}
[[File:Encampment-Concept-NickGindraux.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Concept art of the encampment by Nick Gindraux]]
The Nikto hideout first appeared in "[[Chapter 1: The Mandalorian]],"<ref name="Chapter 1" /> the debut episode of [[Jon Favreau]]'s [[Disney+]] live-action series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''. The episode aired on [[November 12]], [[2019]].<ref name="Insider201">{{InsiderCite|201|Star Wars: The Mandalorian Season One Companion|''Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season One Companion}}</ref> The location was identified in the audio description for "[[Chapter 7: The Reckoning]],"<ref name="Audio Description Chapter 7" /> which aired on [[December 18]], 2019.<ref name="Insider201" /> Prior to the show's release, the location was first shown in a series of promotional photos published on [[StarWars.com]] on [[April 14]], 2019.<ref name="SWCC 2019 1">{{SW|url=news/swcc-2019-see-new-photos-from-the-mandalorian|text=SWCC 2019: See New Photos from ''The Mandalorian''}}</ref><ref name="SWCC 2019 2">{{SW|url=news/swcc-2019-9-things-we-learned-from-the-mandalorian-panel|text=SWCC 2019: 9 Things We Learned from ''The Mandalorian'' Panel}}</ref>

Unlike its surrounding landscape, the encampment itself was a physical set that the actors were filmed in.<ref name="YouTube-BTS">{{YouTube|video=XjUWmGe9hmQ|text='The Mandalorian' Episode 1 Behind the Scenes|channel=@hollywoodstreams|name=hollywoodstreams|quote=Pedro Pascal, Carl Weathers, Producer Jon Favreau, and Director Dave Filoni take us behind the scenes of 'The Mandalorian' Episode 1.}}</ref> As fire was difficult to execute in an interior set, a small walkway was built on the exterior along with pillars for the characters to hide behind. Filming of Chapter 1 took place between [[October 1]]&ndash;[[October 26|26]], [[2018]], while Chapter 7 was filmed between [[October 29]] and November 12 of that year.<ref name="Art of Mandalorian S1" />

Concept designs for the encampment were drawn by [[Ben Grangereau]], [[Christian Alzmann]], [[Doug Chiang]], [[Jama Jurabaev]], [[Nick Gindraux]], [[Ryan Church]], and [[Seth Engstrom]], while [[Russell Paul]] created an overview of the location and the action scene. According to Chiang, the encampment was an abandoned [[mining]] town that the Nikto mercenaries found useful as the structure was hidden and easy to protect. The encampment's design was inspired by the film [[Wikipedia:Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid|''Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid'']], as well as old [[Wikipedia:Spaniards|Spanish]] [[Wikipedia:Mission (station)|missions]]. The film was also used as a reference for the standoff scene between Djarin and IG-11.<ref name="Art of Mandalorian S1" />

===Video game appearances===
[[File:NiktoHideout-Minecraft.png|thumb|right|300px|The Nikto hideout, as it appears in ''Minecraft'']]
On [[April 22]], [[2020]], the encampment was featured in a trailer for the [[Star Wars video games|mobile game]] ''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]'' as part of an announcement that characters from ''The Mandalorian'' would be added to the game.<ref name="Galaxy Heroes Mando Trailer">{{EASWYouTube|g0V7PfBD5bU|Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes &mdash; The Mandalorian}}</ref> On [[December 16]], 2020,<ref name="Beskar Mando Date">{{ThisWeek|VSRBvBhqGVY|Exciting Lucasfilm Announcements, A New Story From The High Republic, and More!|sw_url=video/exciting-lucasfilm-announcements-a-new-story-from-the-high-republic-and-more}}</ref> the location was added to the game as part of a Hero's Journey event for Din Djarin in his full [[Din Djarin's armor|armor]], adapting the events of the show. In the game, the encampment is the setting for that Hero's Journey's first level, in which the player takes control of Djarin and IG-11 to defeat the Nikto mercenaries. Djarin later mans the cannon to defeat the remaining Niktos and break down the entrance in order to find Grogu inside.<ref name="Galaxy Heroes">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]''</ref>

On [[November 16]], 2020,<ref name="Minecraft DLC">{{SW|url=news/minecraft-star-wars-dlc|text=The ''Minecraft Star Wars'' DLC is the Way}}</ref> the encampment was added to the [[Mojang Studios]] video game [[Minecraft Star Wars|''Minecraft'']] as part of the ''Minecraft Star Wars'' expansion pack. In the game, the structure is located on the Arvala-7 section of the map. Grogu can be found in his hovering pram within the innermost building, which can be entered after breaking down the entrance by activating the cannon pointed at it. If the player feeds the infant [[W:c:minecraft:Rabbit Stew|rabbit stew]], he will begin to follow the player.<ref name="Minecraft">''[[Minecraft Star Wars]]''</ref>

